# --- first-party: the scanner scanning itself --------------------------------
# The binary guard used to embed a raw NUL byte, which made the scanner treat
# its OWN source as binary and skip it. Fixed, it now scans itself and matches
# the literals of the rules it defines. Allowed per rule, never per file, so a
# planted GitHub token in either copy is still Critical.
file:bundle/hooks/lib/security-scanner.js + label:private key | the rule source holds the RSA/SSH header literals its own rules search for
file:bundle/hooks/lib/security-scanner.js + label:risk) | the rule labels end in the same call-site text (code-injection / XSS / shell-exec) their rules search for
file:bundle/opencode/hooks/lib/security-scanner.js + label:private key | byte-identical mirror of bundle/hooks/lib/security-scanner.js
file:bundle/opencode/hooks/lib/security-scanner.js + label:risk) | byte-identical mirror of bundle/hooks/lib/security-scanner.js